              "type": "text",
              "text": "If a car travels at an average speed of 60 km/h, it takes 77 minutes to complete a certain trip. To complete the same trip in 84 minutes, what average speed is required?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$55\\text{ km/h}$",
      "worked": "For the same trip, the distance is constant, so speed and time are inversely proportional. With time measured in hours,\n$$\\begin{align*}d&=60\\times\\frac{77}{60}\\\\d&=77\\text{ km}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor the 84-minute trip,\n$$\\begin{align*}v&=\\frac{77}{84/60}\\\\v&=55\\text{ km/h}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
